# The PAD's LENGTH (SEQ, a step held, KNOB 2): a NOTE and TIEs after it; 0 a REST; shorter: its TIEs back to
# RESTs; the first length turns HOLD off (lengths play with it off); a chord sounds its length, whole steps.
# (Holding an empty step writes a NOTE: a length of 1; each detent then adds or takes one.)
wait 300
turn ALGO 3
expect part 3
expect sound2.1.7 1
tap SEQ
key w0 down
turn K2 3
key w0 up
expect gate1.0 1
expect gate1.1 2
expect gate1.2 2
expect gate1.3 2
expect gate1.4 0
expect sound2.1.7 0
shot padlen.png
# shorter: 4 -> 2, steps 3 and 4 back to RESTs
key w0 down
turn K2 -2
key w0 up
expect gate1.1 2
expect gate1.2 0
expect gate1.3 0
# 0: the step a REST, its TIE too
key w0 down
turn K2 -2
key w0 up
expect gate1.0 0
expect gate1.1 0
# a length of 8 on step 1 sounds ~8 steps (a step: 120 ms at 125 BPM) then lets go
key w0 down
turn K2 7
key w0 up
expect gate1.7 2
expect gate1.8 0
# a step the length comes to cover loses its own values (a p-lock on step 5: its lane goes with it), and the
# LENGTH on the screen follows each detent (the knob row's signature has the length in it)
key w0 down
turn K2 -7
key w0 up
expect gate1.0 1
expect gate1.1 0
lane 2 1 0 4 99
expect lanes 1
key w0 down
turn K2 3
key w0 up
expect lanes 1
key w0 down
turn K2 1
wait 120
shot padlen5.png
key w0 up
expect gate1.4 2
expect lanes 0
key w0 down
turn K2 3
key w0 up
expect gate1.7 2
# KNOB 3: the step's CHORD (PAD: the PAD's CHORD, NOTE, MIN7, MAJ7), KNOB 4: its inversion (flags bits 4-5, 6-7)
key w0 down
turn K3 1
turn K4 2
key w0 up
expect bflags1.0 145
key w0 down
turn K3 5
turn K4 -5
key w0 up
expect bflags1.0 49
param 2 1 15 0
param 5 3 1 0
param 5 3 2 0
wav padlen.wav
tap PLAY
wait 1800
tap PLAY
wait 300
wavstop
